# vitabrowser: hand-port fixes to MacSurf's core (cache + build defects)
#
# Hand-maintained patch (like 15-netsurf-redraw-c.patch). These are NOT
# generated: the files are part of the generated MacSurf stack, and the
# fixes correct defects in that generated content. If a generated patch
# ever rewrites a hunk's context, re-apply by hand.
#
# Defects, all found on first clean Linux build (2026-09-21):
#
# llcache.c: macsurf_debug_log_writef is called before any nested-extern
#   declaration, so it needs a file-scope extern. (MacSurf's BAD_INPUT ->
#   BAD_PARAMETER renames and the removal of its local nsu_base64 bodies --
#   which would duplicate libnsutils's base64.c at link -- are already carried
#   by the generated MacSurf-vs-upstream stack; adding them here would make
#   this patch's hunks redundant on the clean path and fail it.)
# hlcache.c: two entry_handle initializers predate the 4th struct field
#   (bool dr_queued); C zero-fills it, -Werror does not.
# utils/file.c: MAC_DIR is a CodeWarrior frontend-shim alias (shims/dirent.h)
#   for DIR *; on Linux use the native DIR.
# desktop/netsurf.c: MacSurf's memset call has no #include <string.h>
#   (CodeWarrior's libc pulled it in implicitly).
#
# Generated: diff -u of the post-stack base files against these exact edits.
# Applies to: netsurf (after the generated stack)
--- a/content/llcache.c
+++ b/content/llcache.c
